The decisive issue is H:

- The paper proves worst-case hardness only for instances produced by its Smooth Label Cover reduction—not for randomly planted noisy halfspaces. [Paper](https://arxiv.org/abs/1707.01795)
- Given a satisfying Label Cover labeling, Section 3.4 constructs the halfspace certificate directly in \(O(|V|)\). Planting that labeling establishes G but does not inherit the paper’s hardness theorem.
- The paper-native structural witnesses can be recovered by polynomial-time coefficient scans, disqualifying Track A.
- The paper provides no separate compact route supporting an honest Track B family.

